WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
Next let's explore the features and usage of AI Context Inspector

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.020
The original motivation behind this tool

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:12.000
is that when creating Rules and Skills for AI

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.880
these files are scattered across different project folders

5
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.600
making them hard to inspect and manage centrally

6
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.080
as well as inconvenient to search or reference

7
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.980
More importantly during active conversations

8
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.240
it is difficult to verify whether AI successfully loaded our rules

9
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.260
or correctly invoked designated skills

10
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:36.320
Therefore I built this tool to provide full visibility into AI context

11
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.940
Opening this tool in the IDE left sidebar

12
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.340
the Active Environment Configuration panel appears first

13
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:47.740
Here you can see all active configurations at a glance

14
00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.940
including Core Rules

15
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.460
Conditional Rules and Skill inventories

16
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.240
while all installed MCP servers are listed below in real time

17
00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:01.100
keeping us fully informed of the current execution environment

18
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.080
Previously these rules and skills used short English IDs

19
00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.700
making it hard to understand their contents at a glance

20
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.100
With this tool we can freely toggle between English and Chinese titles

21
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.140
quickly inspecting detailed documentation and notes

22
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.200
When expanding each item

23
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.800
the tool provides three practical features

24
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.440
First is 'Copy Name

25
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.200
click to paste directly into chat to quickly reference that skill

26
00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.780
Second is 'Reveal in Explorer

27
00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.020
highlighting the exact file location in the file tree

28
00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.620
Third is 'Direct Open

29
00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.960
click to immediately open the file for editing and modifications

30
00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.520
Another powerful flagship feature is 'Recent Conversation Snapshots

31
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.340
To check which rules and skills were referenced in past AI chats

32
00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:48.380
simply select a specific history session from the dropdown menu

33
00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:54.280
and the panel automatically parses and lists all rules and context loaded for that turn

34
00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.180
This feature is extremely practical

35
00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.800
enabling us to audit rule behaviors

36
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.080
and fine-tune trigger conditions for conditional rules

37
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.740
ensuring AI loads the right skills and rules at the right time in every chat
